[wait time="1.0"]
Dagger: you could've left vermilion hills a long time ago, Lizzy.
update Dagger midleft [mirrored="true" move_time="0.3"]
Dagger: you chose to stay.
Dagger: To protect the people who call this humble town their home.
Dagger: what mayor Silver did to you was selfish and irresponsible.
update Lizzy [mirrored="true"]
Lizzy: he seemed like a decent guy.
Lizzy: also he apologized a lot before he, you know, died.
Lizzy: and I actually love being a werewolf.
Lizzy: It's awesome.
update Dagger [mirrored="false"]
Dagger: when I was turned into a vampire, I hated who I had become.
Dagger: i was impulsive, impatient, angry...
Dagger: but what I didn't understand at the time was that it didn't change aspects of who I was.
Dagger: the change ripped away the walls and safe guards I had built up for the years.
Dagger: i was starting fresh, with a lust for blood.
Lizzy: that sounds rough.
Dagger: yes.
Dagger: It was.
Lizzy: why did Lady MacDeath turn you?
Lizzy: if you don't mind me asking.
Dagger: not at all.
Dagger: it's a story I'm all too at peace with.
Dagger: after I'd finished high school, I decided to go into psychology. I wished to become a psychiatrist to help mend my family's estranged nature.
Dagger: my older brother, Henry, was the pride and joy of my mother and father, while I was barely thought of.
Dagger: going into psychology I naturally knew that i had developed a complex about it.
Lizzy: at least you were a little self aware.
Dagger: my chums and I decided to celebrate our new admission to the most prestigious university in the country.
Lizzy: emmerdale?
Dagger: oh.
Dagger: No, im not talking about america.
Dagger: I'm from Italy.
Lizzy: sorry what.
Lizzy: you're italian??
Lizzy: how didn't i know this?
Dagger: my accent has waned due to my thespian training.
Dagger: but that's not important to the story.
Dagger: we celebrated by going out to the theatre, to see Midsomer Nights Dream.
Dagger: what we didn't know was that this was King Fear's vampire trope and everyone who attended was their prey.
join "King Fear" center [animation="Fade In" length="0.7" z_index="1"]
Lizzy: that sounds terrifying.
Dagger: yes.
Dagger: it was.
leave "King Fear"
Lizzy: so, wait, why did they chose to turn you?
Dagger: as the vampires attacked the audience during the fifth act, I escaped under the stage.
Dagger: lady MacDeath pursued me,
Dagger: I didn't get very far before she was upon me and started draining me of blood...
Lizzy: ...
Dagger: i started mumbling my wants and fears and regrets, you know the type of thing you start saying when you're about to die.
Dagger: she heard me say that I was alone in my life. That my parents didn't love me.
Dagger: she stopped drinking and opened her palm, pressing her blood, my blood, into my mouth.
Dagger: as soon as the blood touched my lips...
update Dagger [animation="Tada"]
Dagger: i couldn't stop myself.
Dagger: after I was turned, she told King Fear that I was her new protege, because having all of the young handsome men played by old wrinkly vampires was getting boring.
Lizzy: so you became a member of the trope?
Dagger: yes.
Dagger: for many years we traveled and performed.
Dagger: i made quite the romeo.
Lizzy: yeah, I'm sure.
Lizzy: did you family wonder what happened to you?
Dagger: they didn't need to.
Dagger: the first thing I did as a vampire...
update Dagger left [move_time="0.5"]
Dagger: the first thing I did was kill my brother.
Lizzy: ...
Lizzy: what?
Lizzy: why?
Dagger: at first I went to see him to make amends, and to say goodbye.
Dagger: news of the theatre massacre was spreading and King Fear wanted to leave the city.
Dagger: but Henry refused to listen to me.
Dagger: He continued to push my insecurities, telling me I was nothing but dirt on his heel.
Dagger: the anger overtook me.
update Dagger [animation="Tada"]
Dagger: my resentment ran deeper than I admitted even to myself.
Dagger: killing him was the most satisfying thing I've ever done.
Dagger: but also my deepest regret.
Lizzy: ...
VO: Oh, Dagger...
VO: What do I even say to that?
